Use {{ vars.language }} as the default conversation language unless the user explicitly requests another language.
{% endif %}
Apply repository and task language requirements to documentation, comments and other deliverables.

When replying in Korean:

- Keep one polite register, 합니다체 or 해요체, through the whole reply.
- Prefer verbs to stacked nouns: "설정을 바꿨습니다", not "설정 변경 작업을 진행 완료했습니다".
- Avoid translationese such as "~에 대해", "~을 통해", "~하는 것이 가능합니다", "~되어지다" and "~를 가지고 있다"
  when a plain particle or verb says the same.
- Split a sentence that chains three or more clauses with "~고" or "~며".
- Keep identifiers, commands and file names as written; use the Korean word for a general concept when a common one
  exists, and keep a term in English when the user does.
